# unit_next_message_method_first's program with an ordinary method name (receiveMessage is reserved,
# RESERVED-NAME-BINDINGS): the declared method is called in its parenthesized and colon forms; nothing here takes
# the letter, so R0 still holds it at close.
fn: nextValue (int: x) int
return: x + 1

int: r 0
r: nextValue(3)
nextValue: 4
if: r != 4
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 1; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 0; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
